    decision+='''\n## Defensible D2 design and gates\n\n1. Freeze audit hashes, native-QC policy, target tolerance and eligible source\n   fields. Keep every repeat visit/device/copy of a person in one group. No\n   source-wide row randomization or full-person-trajectory normalization.\n2. Plan a fixed20-person Shanghai holdout and80-person development pool,\n   selected by a seeded source-ID-only participant permutation. No outcomes,\n   window counts or severity metrics drive holdout assignment. Generate a\n   private manifest only in D2. Fivefold grouped development on the80 selects\n   preprocessing, features and models; never tune against the20-person holdout.\n3. Begin with observed glucose/time-of-day only. Demographics/anthropometry\n   require a baseline-availability declaration. Clinical-lab fusion remains a\n   separate noncausal retrospective analysis unless real pre-cutoff dates can\n   be established. Exclude hypoglycemia summary, full-trajectory mean/count\n   and future intake, insulin, activity or treatment-derived summaries.\n4. In D2 compare persistence and causal slope forecasts before more complex\n   models. Use participant-balanced fitting/evaluation; train-only scaling/\n   imputation policy and explicit missing masks. No final model was trained\n   during D1. Forecast target remains observed glucose, not imputed glucose.\n5. Separate cold-start population forecasting from a warm-prefix experiment.\n   For warm personalization reserve each subject’s first48h as calibration\n   context, purge120min between calibration labels and evaluation landmarks,\n   and compute all baselines/meal-response history as ofT. Held-out people\n   remain outside global fitting; prefix use must be declared as the deployment\n   estimand. D1 full-record counts are upper bounds, not post-split/purge counts.\n6. Preserve all14 CGMacros T2D subjects for external domain-shift checks; this\n   is a small pilot, not clinical validation. Resolve source interpolation/\n   observation provenance and causal wearable filtering first. Do not derive\n   native observations by unverified phase downsampling. Choose Libre as\n   the matching15min device only after that gate; Dexcom device sensitivity\n   is paired within person. Never use the dual sensors as two test cohorts.\n7. Treat other Glucose-ML populations and GlucoFM as benchmark references;\n   do not pretrain on their Shanghai or CGMacros copies then claim those\n   people are unseen. Supplied GlucoFM splits fail participant isolation and\n   must be replaced. Underlying interpolation also needs an explicitly\n   different benchmark estimand and cannot substantiate observed-only accuracy.\n8. Shanghai cannot train an HR/activity fusion model because those channels\n   are absent. Keep CGMacros untouched for the primary glucose-only external\n   check. A later14-person multimodal grouped-CV/leave-one-person-out pilot\n   would be a separate exploratory model, and its CGMacros evaluation would\n   not be external validation of that multimodal model. Do not promise\n   learned wearable benefit from these current primary/external roles.\n9. Later report horizon-specific subject-macro MAE/RMSE and clinical error\n   analysis with participant bootstrap intervals. Separate cold-start/warm,\n   demographics/CGM/meal/HR ablations, source/device shifts, missing coverage\n   and incident/existing-high events. Calibration/event threshold selection\n   belongs to development validation only; no test-set performance is in D1.\n10. A demo can replay real Shanghai sensor measurements and same-person\n   context; show model forecasts only after D2 validation. Label unavailable\n   modalities and synthetic FHIR integration explicitly. Never join clinical\n   records from other cohorts or imply current live sensing.\n\n## Leakage tests and verification\n\n`tests/test_metabolic.py` exercises timestamp-based horizons, gap rejection,\nduplicate conflict quarantine, original-order accounting, future-CGM prefix\ninvariance, delayed availability, future/unknown meal-insulin-activity feature\ngates, train-only normalization and person/copy split checks. Synthetic fixture\nvalues validate software invariants only. The D1 completion verifier independently\nre-enumerates Shanghai windows from private canonical records and checks\nall six aggregate reports, raw file hashes, source maps, benchmark split facts\nand output permissions. It does not certify absent real-world receipt data.\n'''
